# Build artefacts
build/
.gradle/
*.apk
local.properties
.idea/

# Signing material. The keystore lives outside the repo entirely, in
# ~/tvs-signing/, and reaches CI only as a base64 secret. These two entries are
# a backstop for a local build that writes them into the tree — a leaked
# keystore cannot be un-leaked, and anyone holding it could sign an "update" to
# this app.
key.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# Captured protocol data — large, and specific to the owner's scooter.
# Share a redacted sample deliberately, never by accident.
captures/
*.btsnoop_hci.log
*.pcap
*.pcapng

# Reverse-engineering scratch space. The official APK and any decompilation of
# it stay OUTSIDE this repository; see research/SOURCES.md.
apk/
*.apk
decompile/
jadx*/

#local folders
ref/
wrapper.log

# Local build transcripts. Machine noise, and they differ on every run, so they
# make the history unreviewable. The interesting evidence belongs in log/ and
# docs/, not in a redirect of stdout. Root-scoped so a deliberate capture
# elsewhere in the tree is not silently swallowed.
/*.log

# Decompiled vendor code (see research/vendor/README.md). Expensive to
# regenerate — hours of CPU on a 2-core budget — so it is kept on disk but
# never committed. The two APKs it came from live in the parent folder and
# are referenced by SHA-256 in research/SOURCES.md.
research/vendor/
